(6582352, 980157, 34192, '<td valign="top">This was my favorite in the challenge.  Admittedly, I didn''t view all the images and didn''t get a chance to get back to it, so I gave it a nine on my first pass.  I think it sets up a wonderful story and allows me to fill in the blanks.  The whole scene is just so interesting and ripe with possibility! The lines here work wonderfully for you.  The only rough spot in the photo is that stupid globulous bush, but its shape and color is echoed by the car so it is tempered a little.  The eye pretty much ignores it anyway - the colors of the man''s shirt, his roses, the barber poles, really pulls the eye back into the action.  It''s like that song - "Anticipation. It''s making me wait."  I know something is going to happen so I sit and watch... Love this, thanks for sharing!</td>', 'This was my favorite in the challenge.  Admittedly, I didn''t view all the images and didn''t get a chance to get back to it, so I gave it a nine on my first pass.  I think it sets up a wonderful story and allows me to fill in the blanks.  The whole scene is just so interesting and ripe with possibility! The lines here work wonderfully for you.  The only rough spot in the photo is that stupid globulous bush, but its shape and color is echoed by the car so it is tempered a little.  The eye pretty much ignores it anyway - the colors of the man''s shirt, his roses, the barber poles, really pulls the eye back into the action.  It''s like that song - "Anticipation. It''s making me wait."  I know something is going to happen so I sit and watch... Love this, thanks for sharing!', '2011-11-02 05:58:53.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582354, 980482, 49018, '<td valign="top">Massively underrated.</td>', 'Massively underrated.', '2011-11-02 06:03:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582355, 980245, 114225, '<td valign="top">I voted this down almost exclusively because of the eyes. Selective saturation (to me) needs to be done in a way that helps tell a story or convey a message. In this photo, I just see it as gimmicky. <br/> <br/>Since the eyes are the most powerful part of a facial portrait, this effect completely removes that power and turns me away.</td>', 'I voted this down almost exclusively because of the eyes. Selective saturation (to me) needs to be done in a way that helps tell a story or convey a message. In this photo, I just see it as gimmicky.  Since the eyes are the most powerful part of a facial portrait, this effect completely removes that power and turns me away.', '2011-11-02 06:04:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582358, 980544, 49018, '<td valign="top">Massively underrated.</td>', 'Massively underrated.', '2011-11-02 06:06:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582360, 980245, 139795, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote on this challenge (new to the site), but to me, the selective saturation processing feels odd for a ''candid'' photo.  Also, giantmike''s comments apply here.</td>', 'I didn''t vote on this challenge (new to the site), but to me, the selective saturation processing feels odd for a ''candid'' photo.  Also, giantmike''s comments apply here.', '2011-11-02 06:08:26.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582362, 980184, 114285, '<td valign="top">I thought this was yours or Penny street, you did well.</td>', 'I thought this was yours or Penny street, you did well.', '2011-11-02 06:09:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582366, 980369, 49018, '<td valign="top">Very underscored. For what is worth, I didn''t really think this was staged. Perhaps the postprocessing is a tadtoo strong, but nothing that disturbing. I found it a pretty interesting image actually.</td>', 'Very underscored. For what is worth, I didn''t really think this was staged. Perhaps the postprocessing is a tadtoo strong, but nothing that disturbing. I found it a pretty interesting image actually.', '2011-11-02 06:13:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582367, 980450, 104009, '<td valign="top">AWESOME job dude what a blast into a new PB with a red!  congratulations man, look at that voting distribution, only 6 votes under 5, who the heck gave this a ONE?  hope you love this pic you''ll be seeing it on your profile for a lonnnnng time :)</td>', 'AWESOME job dude what a blast into a new PB with a red!  congratulations man, look at that voting distribution, only 6 votes under 5, who the heck gave this a ONE?  hope you love this pic you''ll be seeing it on your profile for a lonnnnng time :)', '2011-11-02 06:15:52.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582368, 980245, 3746, '<td valign="top">I agree with previous comment - selective desaturation is a really gimmicky processing technique that rarely, if ever, enhances a photo. I know I have done my fair share of it whilst building my skills and I look back on those images today and shudder!<br/>Regarding the actual subject of the image - pictures of our children, unless very well done, rarely score well - it may be a great shot to you as you have a connection with the child, and we all know that photos of our own kids are the best in the world! Sadly other people don`t have that connection with your subject and thus its sadly overlooked. Thats probably why this shot scored badly - to most voters who spend no more than 4 or 5 seconds on a shot - this is a shot of your kid messing around shoehorned into the challenge - and they scored it as such.<br/> <br/>I am surprised you didn`t get negative comments on the eyes though.<br/> <br/>Hope this helps!</td>', 'I agree with previous comment - selective desaturation is a really gimmicky processing technique that rarely, if ever, enhances a photo. I know I have done my fair share of it whilst building my skills and I look back on those images today and shudder!Regarding the actual subject of the image - pictures of our children, unless very well done, rarely score well - it may be a great shot to you as you have a connection with the child, and we all know that photos of our own kids are the best in the world! Sadly other people don`t have that connection with your subject and thus its sadly overlooked. Thats probably why this shot scored badly - to most voters who spend no more than 4 or 5 seconds on a shot - this is a shot of your kid messing around shoehorned into the challenge - and they scored it as such. I am surprised you didn`t get negative comments on the eyes though. Hope this helps!', '2011-11-02 06:16:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582370, 980017, 104009, '<td valign="top">congrats on your ribbon dude!  SO CLOSE to a new pb....what a thrilling week it must have been!  Too bad I''d seen the shot beforehand i''d have given it a ten and pushed you over the pb line :|<br/> <br/>way to go james!</td>', 'congrats on your ribbon dude!  SO CLOSE to a new pb....what a thrilling week it must have been!  Too bad I''d seen the shot beforehand i''d have given it a ten and pushed you over the pb line :| way to go james!', '2011-11-02 06:18:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582371, 980245, 93565, '<td valign="top">I voted, and I was one of your low votes.<br/>I voted it such because the desat felt contrived and what was left seemed overdone, as well. Very artificial looking.<br/>I''m not normally terribly fond of photos of children, so there''s gotta be a significant connection to a moment conveyed, and I don''t particularly get that here. There is no context conveyed, which is crucial for a successful candid. I would also question the "candidness" of this one, but that''s a whole different argument. It''s also in the awkward overlap between sharp and purposefully blurred. It''s soft, but it looks soft not because you wanted it that way but because that''s all you could do, unintentional, unconnected to the feeling you''re trying to give the viewer.</td>', 'I voted, and I was one of your low votes.I voted it such because the desat felt contrived and what was left seemed overdone, as well. Very artificial looking.I''m not normally terribly fond of photos of children, so there''s gotta be a significant connection to a moment conveyed, and I don''t particularly get that here. There is no context conveyed, which is crucial for a successful candid. I would also question the "candidness" of this one, but that''s a whole different argument. It''s also in the awkward overlap between sharp and purposefully blurred. It''s soft, but it looks soft not because you wanted it that way but because that''s all you could do, unintentional, unconnected to the feeling you''re trying to give the viewer.', '2011-11-02 06:19:01.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582374, 980245, 135744, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by Simms:</b></div><hr/><i> to most voters who spend no more than 4 or 5 seconds on a shot - this is a shot of your kid messing around shoehorned into the challenge - and they scored it as such.<br/></i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>You hit the nail right on the head. <br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2013-07-09 04:18:26.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by Simms: to most voters who spend no more than 4 or 5 seconds on a shot - this is a shot of your kid messing around shoehorned into the challenge - and they scored it as such.  You hit the nail right on the head. ', '2011-11-02 06:25:18.000000', '2013-07-09 05:18:26.000000', 0),
