(6582867, 980108, 50695, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by mcaldo:</b></div><hr/><i> If the idea is to delay the moment the viewer will find the child and therefore the actual point of interest in the photograph, I like it. However, I find this works particularly well when the photograph has some kind of obvious, apparent subject, so that the viewer can relax, just to then suddendly realize that there is another less obvious point of interest and possibly the real subject of the image.<br/>So, perhaps another angle showing maybe more of the faces of the crowd, or the event they are watching if there is an event, and then somewhere the peering face of the child, would have worked better for me. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>a perceptive comment but that''s not Brian''s thing, and I like Brian''s thing.</td>', 'Originally posted by mcaldo: If the idea is to delay the moment the viewer will find the child and therefore the actual point of interest in the photograph, I like it. However, I find this works particularly well when the photograph has some kind of obvious, apparent subject, so that the viewer can relax, just to then suddendly realize that there is another less obvious point of interest and possibly the real subject of the image.So, perhaps another angle showing maybe more of the faces of the crowd, or the event they are watching if there is an event, and then somewhere the peering face of the child, would have worked better for me.   a perceptive comment but that''s not Brian''s thing, and I like Brian''s thing.', '2011-11-02 15:25:49.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582870, 980380, 50695, '<td valign="top">I like the green tint.</td>', 'I like the green tint.', '2011-11-02 15:28:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(6582875, 980549, 20799, '<td valign="top">You got a 10 from me, Anita. Great capture of a beautiful moment, like a dramatic movie scene!<br/>Btw, funny how the PH red winner is on the other side of the world, and the yellow winner is right here in my office. :)</td>', 'You got a 10 from me, Anita. Great capture of a beautiful moment, like a dramatic movie scene!Btw, funny how the PH red winner is on the other side of the world, and the yellow winner is right here in my office. :)', '2011-11-02 15:31:29.000000', NULL, 0),
